class Solution {
  public int selectionProofPositiveInkInvoice(int[] readings, int k) {
    int[] a=readings; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {Set<Integer>sums=new TreeSet<>();class Walk {void visit(int i,int s){if(i==a.length){sums.add(s);return;}visit(i+1,s);visit(i+1,s+a[i]);}}new Walk().visit(0,0);out.addAll(sums);}
    int answer=0;for(int x:out)if(x>0)answer+=x;return answer;
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

Choose any subset of reading positions, including the empty subset, and sum its readings. Produce every distinct achievable sum in ascending order. Equal readings at different positions remain separate choices.

Return the sum of strictly positive values in the derived sequence, or 0 when none exist.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n*2^n); space O(2^n).

